        <p><em>This post was jointly written by Desh and Claude, based on <=
a href=3D"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gYegqWkq98baazm1SlXBf4K8hsj4sSuS=
/view?usp=3Ddrive_link">Desh=E2=80=99s notes</a>.</em></p>

<p>OpenAI released <a href=3D"https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-live=
-1-in-the-api/">GPT-Live-1 in the API</a> yesterday, with launch partners a=
lready using it in production: <a href=3D"https://x.com/usehatchapp/status/=
2098102253106118700">Hatch</a> for customer service calls, <a href=3D"https=
://x.com/Yelp/status/2098110294727999934">Yelp</a> for restaurant reservati=
ons, and <a href=3D"https://x.com/speak/status/2098095986606551481">Speak</=
a> for language tutoring. It is the API version of the model that powers vo=
ice in ChatGPT, Codex, and Work.</p>

<p>OpenAI has not published anything about the architecture, but we can sti=
ll infer a lot from the API, the pricing, the docs, and third-party evals. =
In this post, let us go through what we know and what we can guess.</p>

<div class=3D"glf-guide">
<p><strong>How to read this page.</strong> Everything in the main text is s=
ourced, with links to the docs, tweets, and leaderboards it comes from. Our=
 guesses are kept out of the main text: they appear as <span class=3D"sn-ta=
g">guess</span> notes in the right margin, anchored to the sentence they co=
mment on. On a narrow screen, tap the <span style=3D"color:#0e7a57">=E2=9C=
=A6</span> marker to expand a note inline. Things we could not resolve from=
 public information are called out in amber <strong style=3D"color:#92400e"=
>? Open question</strong> boxes where they come up. When one gets answered,=
 we strike it out and add the answer in place.</p>
<p>The figures are interactive. Figure 1 and Figure 2 play a scripted seque=
nce and can be stepped through; Figure 3 has sliders for the assumptions be=
hind the pricing model; the benchmark charts link to their sources.</p>
</div>

